{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<chat>\n0+1|note: Maria owns the shared scheduler config (also used by the billing export); never change it without asking her.\n1+1|note: User prefers short answers, conventional commits, and no emojis.\n2+1|note: The sync worker's retry logic lives in src/sync/retry.ts; its tests are in tests/test_retry_page.py.\n3+1|note: Account 8841 is the largest customer: 1.2M rows, about 65x the median account; it hit the nightly sync timeout.\n4+1|note: Decision: keep the old CSV header order (id,name,synced_at) because downstream consumers parse by position.\n5+1|note: The billing export runs nightly at 02:00 on the staging box; its logs are in /var/log/export/.\n6+1|note: Test suite: 48 tests, run with `pytest -q`; test_header_order_unchanged is flaky on main (dict iteration order in write_header).\n7+1|note: Release freeze starts 2026-10-09; only fixes for the sync worker and the export header may merge until then.\n8+1|note: The staging box is stagebox; deploys go through `make deploy-staging`, production deploys need Maria's approval.\n9+1|note: Open question: should failed pages be retried 3 times (current) or 5 times with a longer backoff? User leans to keep 3.\n10+1|note: Fixed the retry wrapper to retry only the failed page instead of the whole batch; added tests/test_retry_page.py.\n11+1|note: Todo for next week: write the migration runbook and check the export header test on a clean checkout.\n</chat>"},{"type":"text","text":"Look at message 10 of our chat in full and tell me its date, using your tools, then run `uname -s` in the shell and say which OS this is. Two sentences at most."}]},"session_id":"fixture","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"fixture","timestamp":"2026-10-04T12:21:21.081Z","isReplay":true}
